# Motor models with a non-ideal actuator, for identifying the real robot.
#
# `SimpleMotor` applies the commanded torque exactly. The real drive does not:
# it has a torque constant below the assumed one, a dead band that small
# commands never leave, and a Coulomb friction. `NonidealTorque` carries those
# 3 as fitted parameters, and the motors and closed loops below wrap it the same
# way the ideal ones wrap `SimpleMotor`, so the two can be compared directly.
#
# The calibration scripts in calibration/ fit `k_scale`, `db` and `tau_c`
# together with the plant's inertias and friction to a robot run.
"""
The real actuator: a torque-constant error, a dead band, and a friction that is
LARGER AT REST THAN IN MOTION.

`tau = k_scale * (tau_cmd - db * tanh(tau_cmd / db)) - f(w) * tanh(w / w_eps)`

with the Stribeck friction

`f(w) = tau_c + (tau_s - tau_c) * exp(-(w / w_s)^2)`

so the friction is `tau_s` at rest and falls to `tau_c` once the wheel slides.

WHY THE VELOCITY DEPENDENCE IS NECESSARY. With `tau_s = tau_c` this reduces to
the earlier model, whose friction was the same at every speed. That model cannot
fit the robot. Swept against a 165 s run on 2026-09-18, with everything else
held at its fitted value:

    db [duty]   position RMS [cm]   peak |x| [cm]   (robot 15.8)
      0.010          1.230              16.0
      0.030          1.849              16.7
      0.050          2.978              17.8
      0.077          4.463              19.1   <- the measured break-away
      0.100          5.123              19.7

Monotonic, with no minimum anywhere near the bench value of 0.077 to 0.122 duty.
The direction gives the reason away: a stickier robot should fall SHORT, and
this one sails FURTHER past. A friction that does not depend on speed charges
the full static break-away while the wheel is spinning, so the model cannot
brake. The fit escapes by choosing `db = 0.010 duty`, 8 times below the
measured value, because most of the samples are in the sweep and not in the
holds. That number is therefore not a measurement of the dead band; it is the
least-damaging compromise available to a model of the wrong shape.

What this still does NOT capture is true hysteresis: break-away depending on the
history of approach, and presliding displacement. That needs an internal state,
as in LuGre. `tanh(w / w_eps)` also means the wheel never quite sticks, it
creeps very slowly, so `w_eps` must be small for the holds to look right.
"""
component NonidealTorque
  tau_cmd = RealInput() {^tau_cmd}
  w = RealInput() {^w}
  tau = RealOutput() {^tau}
  "Torque-constant error (1 = ideal)"
  parameter k_scale::Real = 0.85
  "Dead-band width, N*m"
  parameter db::Real = 0.01
  "Coulomb friction torque in motion, N*m"
  parameter tau_c::Real = 0.005
  "Static friction torque at rest, N*m. Equal to tau_c disables the Stribeck term."
  parameter tau_s::Real = 0.005
  "Stribeck speed: how fast the friction falls from tau_s to tau_c, rad/s"
  parameter w_s::Real = 0.1
  "Speed scale of the friction smoothing, rad/s"
  parameter w_eps::Real = 0.5
relations
  tau = k_scale * (tau_cmd - db * tanh(tau_cmd / db)) - (tau_c + (tau_s - tau_c) * exp(-(w / w_s) ^ 2)) * tanh(w / w_eps)
metadata {
  "Dyad": {"icons": {"default": "dyad://BlockComponents/Gain.svg"}},
  "_links": {
    "tau_cmd": {
      "Dyad": {
        "placement": {
          "diagram": {"iconName": "default", "x1": 60, "y1": 300, "x2": 140, "y2": 380, "rot": 0}
        },
        "tags": []
      }
    },
    "w": {
      "Dyad": {
        "placement": {
          "diagram": {"iconName": "default", "x1": 60, "y1": 620, "x2": 140, "y2": 700, "rot": 0}
        },
        "tags": []
      }
    },
    "tau": {
      "Dyad": {
        "placement": {
          "diagram": {"iconName": "default", "x1": 860, "y1": 460, "x2": 940, "y2": 540, "rot": 0}
        },
        "tags": []
      }
    }
  }
}
end

"Planar motor with the `NonidealTorque` actuator model. Plays the real robot in the synthetic study."
component NonidealMotor
  extends MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.PartialTwoFrames
  torquesource = RotationalComponents.Sources.TorqueSource() {^torquesource}
  motor_rotation = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.Revolute(render = false) {^motor_rotation}
  damper = RotationalComponents.Components.Damper(d = d) {^damper}
  fixed = RotationalComponents.Components.Fixed() {^fixed}
  speed = RotationalComponents.Sensors.VelocitySensor() {^speed}
  actuator = NonidealTorque(k_scale = k_scale, db = db, tau_c = tau_c, tau_s = tau_s, w_s = w_s, w_eps = w_eps) {^actuator}
  "Torque command"
  torqueinput = RealInput() {^torqueinput}
  "Viscous friction coefficient"
  parameter d::RotationalDampingConstant = 0.0
  parameter k_scale::Real = 0.85
  parameter db::Real = 0.01
  parameter tau_c::Real = 0.005
  parameter tau_s::Real = 0.005
  parameter w_s::Real = 0.1
  parameter w_eps::Real = 0.5
relations
  connect(torquesource.spline, motor_rotation.flange_a, damper.spline_a, speed.spline) {^id8}
  connect(frame_a, motor_rotation.frame_a) {^id9}
  connect(motor_rotation.frame_b, frame_b) {^id10}
  connect(torquesource.support, damper.spline_b, fixed.spline) {^id11}
  connect(torqueinput, actuator.tau_cmd) {^id12}
  connect(speed.w, actuator.w) {^id13}
  connect(actuator.tau, torquesource.tau) {^id14}
metadata {
